The seeded Rust LIME spike independently reimplements the tabular explanation
algorithm in lime 0.2.0.1, including quartile discretization, empirical category
sampling, the default exponential kernel, auto feature selection and weighted
Ridge. Algorithm references: https://github.com/marcotcr/lime .

LIME copyright (c) 2016 Marco Tulio Correia Ribeiro; BSD-2-Clause license text
accompanies this spike. This code is not the Python lime package. Rust RNG,
distribution arithmetic, solver details and constant-target handling differ as
documented in docs/RUST_SPIKE_LIME.md.

The path dependency netsec-xgboost-spike carries its separate Apache-2.0
TreeSHAP algorithm attribution and license. Cargo.lock pins dependencies; their
copyrights/licenses remain with their respective authors. NumPy's public NPY
format specification guided the bounded numeric reference reader.
